=== Part 1: scheduler tick vs. user creating a cron ===
  user wrote [A, B]
  scheduler wrote [A + lastFiredAt]

  final on disk : ["A"]
  task B (the cron the user just scheduled) exists? false
  -> LOST: the scheduler's stale write overwrote the user's new cron.

=== Part 2: lost lastFiredAt ===
  A.lastFiredAt = 1700000100000
  ids on disk   = ["A","B"]
  -> lastFiredAt survived this run.

NOTE: Part 1/2 sequence the awaits deliberately (the functions have no
      mutual exclusion, so this interleaving is permitted). Part 3 below
      races them without any artificial ordering.
